Assignment 3 — Access Control Logging

Team
Giorgos Karageorgiou — AM 2015030123
Georgios Patsalidis — AM 2006030122

Implementation
The audit_logger.so shared library intercepts fopen(), fwrite() and fclose()
through LD_PRELOAD. It calls the original libc functions, preserves their results
and errno, and appends versioned tab-separated records to /tmp/access_audit.log.
Records contain UID, PID, absolute pathname, UTC timestamp, operation (0 create,
1 open, 2 write, 3 close), permission-denied flag, SHA-256 when safely observable,
and operation outcomes. The logger tracks streams opened by intercepted fopen().
The analyzer reports users denied more than five distinct file paths (-s), or
successful-access users and positive-return fwrite() modification counts for a
specified path (-i). The paths are case-sensitive and lexically normalized.

Requirements (Ubuntu 24.04 or Ubuntu under WSL)
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y gcc make libssl-dev python3

Build
make all

Shared log setup
Provision /tmp/access_audit.log once before running either tool. The following
command deliberately fails if that path already exists, instead of replacing it:

python3 - <<'PY'
import os
path = "/tmp/access_audit.log"
flags = os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW
fd = os.open(path, flags, 0o666)
try:
    os.fchmod(fd, 0o666)
finally:
    os.close(fd)
PY

The log must be an existing regular file, readable and append-writable by all
participating ordinary user accounts (mode 0666 for this laboratory exercise).
Check an existing log's type, owner and permissions before deciding to reuse it.
The logger does not automatically recreate a missing or invalid log.

Demonstration (run as a normal user, never root)
LD_PRELOAD=./audit_logger.so ./test_audit
./audit_monitor -s
./audit_monitor -i /tmp/a3-assignment-XXXXXX/example.txt

Replace XXXXXX with the actual unique directory printed as DEMO_DIR. The program
also prints ANALYZE_FILE, the exact pathname to pass to -i. It creates three
example files, performs real writes and closes, and tests six distinct denied
paths. Permission-denial fixtures are restored and removed after each attempt.
Successful demonstration files remain in the printed temporary directory for
inspection and can be deleted afterward by their owner.

Build cleanup
make clean

Limitations
LD_PRELOAD covers only calls through these three libc functions, not every
system call or unregistered stream. No forced fflush() is performed. Genuine
hashes use OpenSSL EVP on safely readable regular files; otherwise N/A is
recorded, which may differ from the assignment's literal hash requirement.
Counts are qualifying positive fwrite() events, including partial returns, not
necessarily distinct final file contents. Shared mode-0666 logs support ordinary
multi-user reading/appending and flock() coordination but are not tamper-proof.
On log failure the original file operation is preserved, so some audit records
may be lost; diagnostic messages are best-effort. Absolute pathname identity is
lexical rather than physical, so hard links and aliases can have different keys.
